<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- BIO-RPT-004 owns api/features/bio-rpt-004/** only. No ProjectReference to
         Biolog.Api.csproj (one-way dependency, scripts/check-module-project-references.sh) and no
         ProjectReference to bio-idn-001/bio-acc-002/bio-crd-007 either, despite all three being
         real runtime dependencies (the operational-health snapshot reads live Identity/Access/
         CardProduction data): every cross-feature runtime need goes through a narrow gateway
         interface this project defines (Domain/IIdentityHealthGateway.cs,
         Domain/IAccessHealthGateway.cs, Domain/IProductionHealthGateway.cs), implemented by an
         adapter in api/Biolog.Api/Modules/BioRpt004Module.cs - the same shape BIO-RPT-002/
         BIO-RPT-003 already established. All three adapters wrap a PUBLIC or already-
         InternalsVisibleTo-granted repository interface already registered by the dependency's
         own module (IPersonRepository.ListByTenantAsync, IAccessDecisionEventRepository.
         ListForTenantAsync, IProductionJobRepository.ListForTenant) - zero edits to any of their
         owned files.

         Device/Card/Sync health are a disclosed, intentionally-scoped HYBRID gap (BIO-RPT-004-
         AC05's own "or an explicitly documented HYBRID state" allowance): BIO-DEV-001's
         IDeviceRepository, BIO-CRD-005/006's card repositories and BIO-MOB-003's offline-sync
         feature none of them expose a tenant-wide read today (verified by direct inspection, not
         assumed) - see docs/features/bio-rpt-004/README.md "Which sources are wired, and why" for
         the full reasoning. This story does not add a tenant-wide list method to any of those
         three dependencies itself (that would be a cross-story-ownership change needing explicit
         sign-off, not a unilateral addition) - it honestly reports those three panels as
         Simulated/unavailable with a stated reason instead of fabricating a number.

         Namespace root is "OperationalDashboard". No new ADR-0001 canonical identifier type is
         minted - this feature creates no durable aggregate of its own, only a read-time
         projection over already-governed data. -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Api" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Features.OperationalDashboard.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
